UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): GDPR Article 37 requires appointment of a Data Protection Officer when processing is carried out by a public authority, when core activities involve regular and systematic monitoring of data subjects on a large scale, or when core activities involve large-scale processing of special categories of data. The requirement is based on the nature and scale of processing.
Wrong (A): The GDPR does not use employee headcount thresholds to determine DPO requirements. The trigger is the type and scale of data processing.
Wrong (B): Processing EU residents'' data triggers GDPR obligations generally, but a DPO is only required under the specific conditions in Article 37.
