-- Q3722: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under HIPAA (45 CFR Section 164.502(b)(2)), the minimum necessary standard does not apply when a covered entity discloses PHI to the individual who is the subject of the information. When a patient requests their own records, the entity must provide access to the designated record set without restriction.
Wrong (B): Providing only specifically requested records applies the minimum necessary standard, which is explicitly exempted for individual access requests under the Privacy Rule.
Wrong (C): The minimum necessary standard does not limit disclosures to the data subject. Denying a patient''s request on this basis misapplies the rule.
