-- Q3727: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per GDPR Article 7 and Recital 32, consent must be freely given, specific, informed, and demonstrated by a clear affirmative action. The controller must prove consent was obtained, and the data subject may withdraw consent at any time as easily as it was given.
Wrong (B): Bundling consent with terms of service without separate indication undermines the "freely given" requirement. GDPR requires consent to be distinguishable from other matters.
Wrong (C): Implied consent through continued service use does not constitute valid consent under GDPR. Pre-ticked boxes, silence, and inactivity are explicitly excluded.
Wrong (D): Consent is one of six lawful bases for all processing under Article 6, not solely required for special categories. Special categories under Article 9 require explicit consent.$EXPL$
